description:
File: crates/kithd/src/lib.rs, line 213

The blob_download_handler calls state.store.lock().unwrap() without handling lock poisoning:

    let guard = state.store.lock().unwrap();
    guard.get_peer_mailbox_for_blob(&blob_id)

If the lock is poisoned (from a previous panicked task), this unwrap() will panic and crash the HTTP handler for that request.

Fix: Match on Err and return INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, matching the pattern already used at line 268 in the same function:

    let guard = match state.store.lock() {
        Ok(g) => g,
        Err(_) => return (StatusCode::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, "store error").into_response(),
    };
    guard.get_peer_mailbox_for_blob(&blob_id)
